  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the retrieval:\n\n**Error origin** \u2014 `pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`: the `legacyProvider.PostStartHook()` registers `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"`, races the ClusterIP repair controller and NodePort repair controller (via `async.Runner`), and returns `errors.New(\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\")` if both haven't signaled `onFirstSuccess` within 1 minute.\n\n**Propagation chain**:\n1. `pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go` (`RepairIPAddress.RunUntil`\u2192`runOnce`\u2192`doRunOnce`\u2192`syncService`) and `pkg/registry/core/service/portallocator/controller/repair.go` are the two controllers being raced; the IPAddress repair path is what issues the `IPAddresses().Create()` call that can come back `Forbidden`.\n2. `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/handler.go` (`Handler.WaitForReady`, 10s timeout) and `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/webhook/generic/webhook.go` (`Dispatch`) are the generic admission-readiness gate \u2014 this is the exact source of `admission.NewForbidden(attr, fmt.Errorf(\"not yet ready to handle request\"))`, hit when a freshly-started apiserver's webhook/namespace informers haven't synced yet.\n3. `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/hooks.go` wires each PostStartHook into a `poststarthook/<name>` readyz check (and `klog.Fatalf`s the whole process if the hook eventually returns an error); `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/healthz.go` and `.../server/healthz/healthz.go` implement `AddBootSequenceHealthChecks`/`informer-sync`, matching the two failing checks in the ticket's readyz output.\n4. `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/config.go` shows the paired `\"generic-apiserver-start-informers\"` hook that the `informer-sync` checker depends on.\n\n**Race condition** \u2014 `pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/cidrallocator.go` (`MetaAllocator`) and `pkg/controlplane/instance.go` (the `start-kubernetes-service-cidr-controller` hook creating the default `ServiceCIDR`) show why a mixed v1.32/v1.33 upgrade window is racy: a freshly-started node's informers/webhook config/ServiceCIDR readiness haven't converged yet when the repair loop tries to (re)create IPAddress objects, so the create is transiently forbidden until caches catch up \u2014 self-resolving once all nodes are on the same version.",
